1. Create a directory : mkdir karate-docker , cd karate-docker
2. Create JS application - nano app.js
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.writeHead(req.url === '/invalid' ? 404 : 200,
        { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
    if (req.url === '/')
        res.end(JSON.stringify({ message: 'Hello from JavaScript Docker Application' }));
    else if (req.url === '/health')
        res.end(JSON.stringify({ status: 'OK' }));
    else
        res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Not Found' }));
}).listen(5000, () => console.log('Server running on port 5000'));
Ctrl+o,enter,ctrl+x
3. Create Dockerfile : nano Dockerfile
FROM node:20
WORKDIR /app
COPY app.js .
EXPOSE 5000
CMD ["node", "app.js"]
4.Build docker image : docker build -t javascript-docker-app:1.0 .
5. Run the docker container : docker run -d --name javascript-app -p 5000:5000 javascript-docker-app:1.0
6. Verify the container : docker ps
7. Test the application manually
 curl http://localhost:5000
 curl http://localhost:5000/health
 curl http://localhost:5000/invalid
8. Create a karate test directory : mkdir karate-test, cd karate-test
9. Create nano docker-app.feature
Feature: Test Dockerized JavaScript Application

  Scenario: Verify home page
    Given url 'http://localhost:5000'
    When method get
    Then status 200
    And match response.message contains 'Hello from JavaScript Docker Application'

  Scenario: Verify health endpoint
    Given url 'http://localhost:5000/health'
    When method get
    Then status 200

  Scenario: Verify invalid endpoint
    Given url 'http://localhost:5000/invalid'
    When method get
    Then status 404
10. Download karate standalone jar : wget -O karate.jar https://github.com/karatelabs/karate/releases/download/v2.1.3/karate-2.1.3.jar
11. Verify the jar exists - ls -lh karate.jar
12. Run the karate test - java -jar karate.jar docker-app.feature
13. View karate test report - xdg-open target/karate-reports/karate-summary.html
